cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Token X-ray or its measurements, please cite it as below."
title: "Token X-ray: measuring the gradient weight training loops give every token"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dhola
    given-names: Kaushik
version: 0.1.2
license: MIT
url: "https://tokenxray.pages.dev/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/kaushikdhola/token-xray"
repository-artifact: "https://pypi.org/project/token-xray-ml/"
abstract: >-
  Token X-ray runs a library's own, unmodified training loop on a tracer model and reads back the gradient
  weight every target token actually received, then compares it with the weight the objective intends.
  It also measures whether gradient leaks from one packed document into another. Real runs cover the
  transformers Trainer, TRL's SFT, DPO and GRPO trainers, and data-parallel training under torchrun; every
  check is mutation-tested.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - training
  - gradient accumulation
  - sequence packing
  - transformers
  - TRL
  - GRPO
  - DPO
